cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Antipsychotic Medication Cost-Effectiveness and Budget Tool"
version: "vS (validation version, September 2026)"
date-released: 2026-09-30
authors:
  - name: "Clinton Health Access Initiative, Mental Health Team"
  - family-names: "Aldridge"
    given-names: "Luke"
    affiliation: "Clinton Health Access Initiative"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chai-luke/mh-cea-tool"
url: "https://medcetool.com"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Browser-based cost-effectiveness and budget impact model for antipsychotic
  medicines in psychosis care, with country inputs for Ethiopia, Nigeria, Rwanda
  and South Africa. Every input is editable and exportable so ministries can run
  the model on their own data. Public version, validation release September 2026.
keywords:
  - cost-effectiveness analysis
  - budget impact
  - antipsychotics
  - schizophrenia
  - mental health
  - health technology assessment
  - essential medicines
